 brother julian and her husband  sean refused to tell her the truth  and bring things to an end the second  season shifts from a family dealing with  a tragedy  to a group of bad people making bad  decisions  in order to try to get a child that they  know isn't theirs to begin with back  in order to keep a lie going it also  fills in the details of leanne's awful  childhood  she had a self-centered abusive mother  who would never give her what she craved  most her acceptance and love even with  the king cake her mother always found  the baby  so that she could say she was special  and use that as a reason to put leanne  down  even though now we see that leanne is in  fact special  she's still in search of a mother's love  and in the end that does turn out to be  the big twist  despite everything that happened despite  her concerns that dorothy was incapable  of taking care of the baby  her act of saving leanne fulfilled that  desire  and now leanne wants to stay with the  turners and create a family  so to recap what happened in the finale  it does pick up right where  episode 9 left off aunt josephine at the  front door  with the betamax machine in tow and  leanne watching from jericho's room  holding the doll  shawn and dorothy let her in she tries  to comfort dorothy  who really only wants the baby back and  when they ask about aunt may and uncle  george she says they're not involved in  this anymore  dorothy agrees to let her talk to leanne  and when she hears that leanne wants to  stay there  she assures her that they don't love her  and we get the idea that as confused as  leanne  is the idea of going back to the church  of the lesser  saints doesn't sound like a great idea  at the same time it's clear that they  still have  some power over her aunt josephine goes  to tell dorothy that her and leanne are  leaving tonight but tells her that she  made a promise that she wants to keep so  she hands her the onesie  that we saw back in season one and when  asked she says it's the truth  and it almost looks like dorothy's gonna  wake up here she's gonna remember what  happened  she locks herself in the room we see  that sean's phone stops working  and then he gets locked in the other  room and it starts to look like leanne  isn't the only person in the house who  has powers  probably my favorite thing in the finale  on the first watch  was the betamax it definitely gave off  some lost  dharma initiative vibes and aunt  josephine's showing her this  as a warning about what will happen if  she doesn't ask for forgiveness  so now we understand what uncle george  was doing in love shack there's an  invocation a consecration  and then an emancipation and essentially  this is something that they need to do  when one of their members leaves the  cult or loses their way  the fact that he talks about taking out  their eyes makes it sound like this is  what roscoe saw  when he was with them we heard him  talking about taking out the  eyes and throwing them away when he was  hypnotized and i don't know about you  but if it was me  i would definitely do whatever aunt  josephine said in order to avoid this  ritual and at first that is what leanne  does  but things fall apart when leanne won't  say that she'll forget dorothy turner  and josephine says it's a sin to covet  someone even a mother  and then she splashes her in the eyes  with the liquid from the wooden box  and goes downstairs to start the  invocation  listening to pennies from heaven and  stabbing herself  repeatedly in the thigh with a fork  really fun stuff  dorothy is not having fun she's actually  decided that she's going to kill herself  and it leads to a pretty emotional  conversation between her and sean  as a couple people who have been  consistently making bad decisions  and doing bad things it was a little  surprising how much this scene actually  worked  downstairs leanne has made it to the  basement and josephine  is pursuing she tries to escape it  doesn't work  and now that the invocation has been  completed and josephine continues with  the ritual  which involves a gruesome slashing of  the limbs  to everyone's surprise dorothy shows up  hits her with a shovel  and saves the anne and for this leanne  says  look she wanted you to think he's gone  he's not gone i'm gonna bring him back  to you  it's what dorothy has been waiting to  hear when she leaves we hear leanne say  she protected me  like i'm her daughter and again this  really landed like a gut punch  think about how bad your relationship  with your family had to be  how bad of an experience being with the  cult would have to have been  in order for you to still really want  dorothy to be your mother  and josephine's down but she's not out  she does come back as leanne is  heating the knife over the pyre that she  lit the one that uncle george left there  a couple episodes back but in the end  leanne gets the upper hand  she stabs her right through the eye and  we don't see it it happens off screen  but it looks like she throws her on the  fire  and then one way or another gets her  upstairs where we see  her charred body in the crawl space  between the walls  after everything that happened sean is  finally ready to tell dorothy the truth  he's right there it's the next thing  he's about to say  and of course dorothy doesn't want to  hear anything she's just waiting for the  baby to come back  and she turns on the baby monitor and  she hears  leanne singing so they go into the  baby's room and lo and behold there she  is  she's wearing a coat and she's holding  the baby in her arms  and she gives him to dorothy there's  really no explanation of how she did  this  the fact that she's wearing the coat  makes it look like she went outside  after stashing aunt josephine's body  however she did that but at this point  it really doesn't matter because  yeah she has power so something related  to her powers made this all possible  the big takeaway is that she says now we  can be a family  so dorothy gets what she wants she gets  the baby back  and what she wants is what shawn wants  basically and leanne's been saved by  dorothy  which translates to her as a mother's  love  the little girl inside her the pageant  contestant the one who saw dorothy  and imagine this wonderful mother who  was so much better than her own  has decided to leave the cult behind and  make this her family  it's not a happy ending though we hear  her say  i don't know why i keep doing bad things  i can feel the dark thing inside me  getting bigger we see the lights flicker  in the room and the house and then we  see that go down the block  she says i'm tired of everyone telling  me what's wrong with me maybe there's  nothing wrong maybe this is who i  am and then she says i know how this  works  i know they're coming from me don't  worry i'll be ready  i know killing you referring to aunt  josephine  started a war and so season two ends  with the answer that yes leanne has  powers and the question becoming then  where do these powers come from we've  seen both uncle george  and aunt josephine appear to have some  powers of their own  does that mean everyone in the cult has  that and probably more importantly  where does that power come from we hear  them refer to a hymn  and the easy answer there is that  they're referring to a god  but perhaps there is an actual person  someone above aunt josephine that we're  gonna meet next season  a pretty healthy balance of answered  questions and ongoing mystery  i definitely like the idea that the big  question  shifts to being more about leanne about  who she is how she has these powers what  she's capable of  than just being about jericho i thought  they did a pretty good job of circling  back  and pulling on some of those threads  that have been dangling there since the  beginning  i think there's a pretty good chance  that julian got leanne  pregnant we didn't see any julian in the  finale and then getting together se